{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Reclassified bug -> task: self-conceded cost/design improvement, not a violated contract\n\nThis ticket's own scope note concedes the classification: story `c1de-d6a0-6cef-4135`'s AC scopes the 20 ms budget to the QUIET case (\"`maybe_drain` no-ops with no spawn **when nothing soaked**, within `DRAIN_GATE_BUDGET_MS` (20 ms)\"), and the ticket text itself concludes \"A gate that finds a real backlog is not on that no-op path, so this is a **cost/design** improvement, not a violated contract — size it accordingly.\" The marker's all-or-nothing write is also exactly what f400's open question #3 sketches as a DESIGN change wanting a plan and review, not a drive-by patch.\n\nNo documented contract is violated by the current behaviour, so this is task-shaped work (a designed improvement with a plan-review), not a defect. The measurements and ACs remain valid and unchanged. Type changed bug -> task; nothing else edited."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787333914594658001,"uuid":"553fde60-09aa-4ae9-b0ac-ada746885973"}